{
  "paraphrase": "For all functions f and g from the real numbers to the real numbers, if f and g are non-constant, differentiable, satisfy the equation f(x + y) = f(x)f(y) - g(x)g(y) for all real numbers x and y, and have f'(0) = 0, then for all real numbers x, (f(x))^2 + (g(x))^2 = 1."
}
